===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|reding}}, {{m|enm|redyng}}, {{m|enm|redand}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rǣdende}}, present participle of {{m|ang|rǣdan|t=to read}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|read|-ing|id2=participial}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{present participle of|en|read|nocat=1}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|reding}}, {{m|enm|redynge}}, {{m|enm|redunge}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rǣding|t=reading}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|read|-ing|id2=gerund noun}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# The process of interpreting written language.
#: {{usex|en|The student is behind in his '''reading''' by several chapters.}}
# {{senseid|en|process of interpreting a symbol}} The process of interpreting a symbol, a sign or a measuring device.
# A value indicated by a measuring device.
#: {{usex|en|He glanced across and took note of the speedometer '''reading'''.}}
#* '''2019''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20190311070055/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/south-korea-proposes-rain-project-with-china-to-cut-pollution/4819207.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: He noted that fine dust '''readings''' have been higher in Seoul than in Beijing recently.
#*:: {{audio|en|He noted that fine dust readings have been higher in Seoul than in Beijing recently.ogg|Audio (US)}}
# An event at which written material is read aloud.
#: {{usex|en|I attended a poetry '''reading'''.}}
# An [[interpretation]].
#: {{usex|en|That's my '''reading''' of the current situation.}}
# A [[spelling]] that intends to indicate the approximate [[pronunciation]] of a word from another language; a [[romanization]], [[transcription]], and/or [[transliteration]].
#* {{quote-journal
